  "description": "I am a physicist with an MS in Physics from the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, where I also taught as a Graduate Teaching Assistant. My research lies in condensed matter physics: spintronics, magnetization and domain-wall dynamics, spin waves and the Landau-Lifshitz-Gilbert equation, exploring how the spin of electrons can be used to build new electronic devices. I am passionate about teaching and about sharing my love for physics.",
